<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-28",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-28",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "treadmill with fan",
      "treadmill with built in fan",
      "treadmill with cooling fan",
      "best treadmill with fan",
      "treadmill console fan",
      "folding treadmill with fan",
      "sole treadmill fan",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: Sole F65", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Treadmills With a Built-In Fan</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        A console fan is one of the most searched treadmill extras and one of the least explained. We kept only the seven treadmills whose Amazon listing or maker spec actually names a built-in fan, from a $387 auto-incline folder to a 22-inch-wide Horizon, and we are honest about what that small fan can and cannot do.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 28, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">How we chose: makers’ published specifications and manuals, independent reviews and owner reports, cross-checked. Not tested hands-on.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We may earn a commission when you buy through the links below. It costs you nothing and never decides a ranking. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#sole-f65"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31qNRVPVU1L._SL500_.jpg" alt="Sole F65" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#sole-f50"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31jT2QJvdZL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Sole F50" width="500" height="333" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#horizon-7-4-at"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41wMaZFsNwL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Horizon 7.4 AT" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Sole F65 · Sole F50 · Horizon 7.4 AT</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Plenty of treadmills have a small fan in the console, but many listings never say so, and a
          few that shout &ldquo;fan included&rdquo; in the title mean a clip-on fan in the box. We searched
          Amazon for treadmills with a fan on 28 November 2026, read the title and bullet points of every
          candidate, checked SOLE&rsquo;s and Horizon&rsquo;s own product data where we could, and kept only
          the seven where a built-in fan is stated in writing. The SOLE F65 is the pick for most people at
          $1,199.99; the THERUN 15% auto-incline folder is the cheapest at about $387. We have not tested
          these treadmills hands-on. Every figure on this page comes from the Amazon listing or the maker&rsquo;s
          site, and each card says where the fan is named and what the listing leaves out.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Overall:</span> <a href="#sole-f65">Sole F65</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Budget:</span> <a href="#therun-15-auto-incline">THERUN 15% Auto Incline Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
